#!/usr/bin/env python3
# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-
"""Computational experiment driver for block-structured mixed-integer optimization.

The DCAP-like study supports three-resource homogeneous-A0 instances, masked
continuous tails, and frozen family-chain configurations with structural audits.
SMKP and GA-like generators are also available through the existing CLI.

Implemented methods are P1 with sharp l1 augmented-Lagrangian cuts and
Pessoa-style In-Out stabilization, the P1-no-rho ablation, the P2 residual-driven
augmented-Lagrangian baseline, and the direct Gurobi extensive form.
The inner oracle supports exact grouped full-matrix reverse-norm cuts and
separate lower/upper bounds; decomposed fixed-z audits provide primal bounds.
Instance generation, panel/family-chain execution, screening, and CSV/JSON
reporting are included in this standalone driver.

The SMKP mode follows the remove-only two-stage model of Tönissen, van den Akker,
and Hoogeveen (2017), using negative expected reward as the minimization objective.
Its scenario-range completion follows the many-scenarios benchmark direction;
it does not claim to reproduce undisclosed Table 8 instance data.
"""

from __future__ import annotations

